# What must not enter the build context.
#
# ── fixtures/ is the one that matters ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# It holds **real client documents** from a live scheme — a title deed, a brief, a priced cost
# plan. README says the repository stays private until they are anonymised. An image is a far
# looser thing than a private repository: it gets pushed to a registry, pulled onto build agents,
# and cached in layers that outlive the tag. None of that is a place for a client's title deed.
#
# Everything else here is either a secret, a build artefact, or weight.

# Secrets. `.env.example` is the only one that may travel.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Real client data (README: "the repository stays private until they are anonymised").
fixtures/

# Rebuilt inside the image; copying them in is slower and risks a host/container mismatch on
# native modules.
node_modules/
.next/
.vercel/
.storage/

# History and CI. A layer holding the whole repository history is weight nobody unpacks.
.git/
.github/
.githooks/

# The browser suites drive a running server from outside it — they are never in the image, and
# puppeteer's bundled Chromium would double its size if they were.
checks/
test-results/

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Documentation. Read in the repository, not shipped to production.
*.md
!README.md
design/
docs/
